{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"anxious-resistant-urson","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Problem\n\nChange 1996 (`02f71da097`, RP-05 S5) added two steps to `.github/workflows/_optionality.yml`\nthat invoke repository files, **without the if-present guard this repo mandates for exactly\nthis case**:\n\n```yaml\n- name: parser-derived docs are byte-current on the lean wheel\n  run: |\n    /tmp/clean/bin/python scripts/gen_cli_help.py --check\n    /tmp/clean/bin/python scripts/gen_cli_reference.py --check\n\n- name: clean-wheel distribution + every-help-form byte contract (portable pytest)\n  run: |\n    /tmp/clean/bin/python -m pytest ... tests/interfaces/contracts/test_cli_registry_distribution.py -rs\n```\n\n`tests/interfaces/contracts/test_cli_registry_distribution.py` was **created by that same\ncommit** (141 lines, new file).\n\n## Mechanism\n\nGerrit's verify job takes the workflow **DEFINITION** from the target branch but checks out the\n**CHANGE'S** tree. So a step added on `main` runs against every open change whose base predates\nit. The test file is absent in those trees, pytest collects nothing, and exits 4:\n\n```\ncollected 0 items\n============================ no tests ran in 0.01s ============================\n##[error]Process completed with exit code 4.\n```\n\nThat is a `Verified -1` caused by the gate, not by the change under review.\n\n## Measured blast radius — 3 open changes, all innocent\n\nFailing the identical job at 34-47s, none of them touching the CLI registry or packaging:\n\n| change | subject |\n|---|---|\n| 1997 | Resolve access-check client seam at call time |\n| 1998 | Stop absent-string child oracles failing open |\n| 1999 | Fail closed on stale KNOWN_ENV_HELPERS rows |\n\n`main` itself is green: \"Optional-Dependency Isolation (mirror)\" and the full \"Test Suite\n(mirror)\" both succeeded, and the whole job reproduces clean locally against `origin/main` in a\nno-extras venv (`rebar --help` exit 0; agents-absent assertion OK; 17 passed).\n\n## The remedy already exists in this repo\n\nThis hazard is documented (ticket `ee2a`, bug `1909-c1a7-9f20-440f`) and every other\nscript-invoking gate step carries the guard. From `_build-and-test.yml`:\n\n```yaml\n- name: comment-hygiene gate\n  run: |\n    if [ ! -f scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py ]; then\n      echo \"not in checked-out tree (change predates the gate) — skipping;\" \\\n           \"the gate re-enforces on rebase and on every post-merge change\"\n      exit 0\n    fi\n    python scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py\n```\n\nThe Verified-gate parity gate and the raw-git-write gate use the same shape. The two new\noptionality steps are the outliers.\n\n## Why this is a defect and not a nuisance\n\nA gate that reds a change for a reason unrelated to the change **trains reviewers to discount\nthe gate**. That is the failure mode `recheck` discipline exists to prevent: once a `-1` can\nmean \"your base is old\", every `-1` becomes ambiguous, and the two-vote gate loses its meaning\nas evidence. The cost is already visible — three unrelated changes, each of whose authors must\notherwise investigate a failure that is not theirs.\n\n## Scope\n\nAdd the established if-present guard to the two new steps. Match the existing wording so the\nskip is self-explaining.\n\nExplicitly OUT of scope: changing what the steps check, weakening either `--check`, or altering\nthe distribution contract. The steps are correct; only their unguarded invocation is wrong.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Both new steps skip with an explanatory message when their target file is absent from the\n      checked-out tree, matching the existing guard wording — verified by a test or a CI dry-run\n      against a tree lacking the file\n- [ ] Both steps still run and still fail on a tree that DOES contain the file, so the guard\n      cannot be satisfied by simply never running — verified by a positive case\n- [ ] A change based on pre-`02f71da097` `main` passes the optionality lane — verified against\n      one of 1997/1998/1999 before their rebase, or an equivalent reconstruction","id":"5bc6-5496-4e17-403a","parent_id":"","priority":1,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"New optionality gate steps lack the if-present guard, so every open change with an older base fails Verified"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787319737933453001,"uuid":"13c1f517-46fa-47db-a08c-e0ffa049c708"}